(7265593, 1129964, 86447, '<td valign="top">To me... *sigh*<br/> <br/>The strongest angle in this image is the "nose" looking one... to the left.   It appears to be about 70 degrees.   <br/> <br/>I like the image very much... but... <br/> <br/>One of my favorite photographer friends here on DPC once told me that... the eye will always go to the lightest part of the image... and the lightest, largest part is... that angle that points to the left edge. <br/> <br/>Unfortunately, it''s not a right angle.   <br/> <br/>Still... I love this image... just not for the challenge topic, despite the fact that there are many, many minor right angles everywhere.   *sigh*</td>', 'To me... *sigh* The strongest angle in this image is the "nose" looking one... to the left.   It appears to be about 70 degrees.    I like the image very much... but...  One of my favorite photographer friends here on DPC once told me that... the eye will always go to the lightest part of the image... and the lightest, largest part is... that angle that points to the left edge.  Unfortunately, it''s not a right angle.    Still... I love this image... just not for the challenge topic, despite the fact that there are many, many minor right angles everywhere.   *sigh*', '2014-09-24 00:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
