(7265715, 1129935, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by backdoorhippie:</b></div><hr/><i> Not crazy about the perspective through the hole.  It is a hole, right? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>No. It is a mirror on a table with the focus on the far reflected image, so the table is totally out of focus. A similar effect as this:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=906685" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1250/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_906685.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1250/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_906685.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1250/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_906685.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i>Angels? Here? <br/> <br/>Even if I look at this image (which I really, really do like, by the way) with the topic at hand... the lines that come to me first and stay with me ... are the angled ones that look like about 45 degrees... <br/> <br/>The 90 degree ones are... secondary. <br/> <br/>But, I''ve been called crazy before. *grin*</i></td></tr></table> <br/>You are right. I sometime look at what we do here as challenging both the photographer and the viewer alike.</td>', 'Originally posted by backdoorhippie: Not crazy about the perspective through the hole.  It is a hole, right?  No. It is a mirror on a table with the focus on the far reflected image, so the table is totally out of focus. A similar effect as this:  Originally posted by Lydia:Angels? Here?  Even if I look at this image (which I really, really do like, by the way) with the topic at hand... the lines that come to me first and stay with me ... are the angled ones that look like about 45 degrees...  The 90 degree ones are... secondary.  But, I''ve been called crazy before. *grin* You are right. I sometime look at what we do here as challenging both the photographer and the viewer alike.', '2014-09-24 10:05:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7265738, 1129923, 104230, '<td valign="top">I love the initial ambiguity of orientation that resolves when your eye moves over to the upper right. Perfect for this challenge. Congratulations on the ribbon.</td>', 'I love the initial ambiguity of orientation that resolves when your eye moves over to the upper right. Perfect for this challenge. Congratulations on the ribbon.', '2014-09-24 10:57:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7265739, 1129930, 170281, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo.  I appreciated the interpretation of the theme and added imagery from the shadows which are well placed in the photo as to not distract from the layout of the bricks but rather add value.  It may have scored better in the shadows challenge, but many of the photos in this challenge also relied on perspective, reflection, shadows, etc.  I really like this image.  Keep up the great work.</td>', 'Very nice photo.  I appreciated the interpretation of the theme and added imagery from the shadows which are well placed in the photo as to not distract from the layout of the bricks but rather add value.  It may have scored better in the shadows challenge, but many of the photos in this challenge also relied on perspective, reflection, shadows, etc.  I really like this image.  Keep up the great work.', '2014-09-24 10:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
